Walks rows where embedding IS NULL and calls the Gemini embedding API to fill them.
Default is a dry-run that prints row count + cost estimate. Pass --apply to write.

Usage:
  orchestrator backfill-embeddings [flags]

Flags:
      --apply              actually call the API and write embeddings (default is dry-run)
      --batch-size int     rows per batchEmbedContents call (capped at 100) (default 100)
  -h, --help               help for backfill-embeddings
      --include-archived   include archived rows (default skips them)
      --limit int          process at most N rows (0 = no cap)
      --max-retries int    per-batch retry ceiling on 429 / 5xx (default 5)
      --quiet              suppress per-batch progress lines
      --rpm int            target requests per minute (0 = no throttle) (default 60)
      --since duration     only consider rows created within this window (e.g. 720h); 0 = all rows

Global Flags:
      --domain string         task domain (dev/personal/work/creative/academic) (default "dev")
      --dry-run               show plan without executing
      --max-turns int         max agentic turns per worker (0 = use persona-aware default)
      --model string          force model for all workers
      --nanika-dir string     path to nanika directory (default: ~/nanika)
      --personas-dir string   path to personas directory (default: ~/nanika/personas/)
      --sequential            force sequential execution
  -v, --verbose               verbose output
